# Webshare live-test credentials.
#
# Copy this file to `.env`. The live Webshare Electron test loads that ignored
# file before it starts. Use either the API token or the username/password pair;
# when both are present, the API token takes precedence.

WEBSHARE_API_KEY=

# WEBSHARE_USERNAME=
# WEBSHARE_PASSWORD=

# These defaults match Webshare's rotating proxy endpoint.
WEBSHARE_PROXY_HOST=p.webshare.io
WEBSHARE_PROXY_PORT=80
WEBSHARE_PROXY_COUNTRIES=us

# Optional comma-separated public URLs for the live replay.
# PIPELINE_LIVE_WEBSHARE_HOSTS=https://www.tripadvisor.com/,https://www.mlive.com/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser Use cloud browser (the paid last acquisition rung).
#
# The rung ships disabled and its call budget defaults to zero, so filling these
# in does not by itself spend anything: the budget in Settings -> Research &
# Acquisition is the switch. Leave every secret blank in this file.

# The API key for the opt-in live smoke check below. The application does not
# read this credential; enter and save its Browser Use key in Settings ->
# Research & Acquisition instead.
BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=

# The exit country to request: a two-letter code, or `none` to run unproxied.
# Unset takes the provider's own default.
# BROWSER_USE_PROXY_COUNTRY=none

# Hosts a control (CDP) endpoint may live on: an exact host, or a leading-dot
# suffix of at least two labels. Defaults to `.browser-use.com`, matching the
# provider endpoint observed by the opt-in live smoke check.
# BROWSER_USE_CDP_HOST_ALLOWLIST=.browser-use.com

# --- Live smoke check only. Never read by the application. ---
#
# `npm run test:live:browser-use` performs at most ONE create/connect/stop
# lifecycle against the real API and therefore costs real money. It refuses to
# run unless both of these are set. The second is an **alarm, not a cap**: the
# provider reports a cost only after a session stops, so it cannot prevent a
# bill — it decides when the run is reported as unexpectedly expensive.
# PIPELINE_LIVE_BROWSER_USE=1
# PIPELINE_LIVE_BROWSER_USE_ALARM_MICROS=20000
#
# `npm run test:live:providers` also collects the Browser Use regression replay,
# which reads every URL a research run failed on and acquires each one once —
# so it costs money per URL. It needs the two switches above plus a cohort: this
# names a JSON file holding an array of URLs. Unset, the replay skips. Set but
# unreadable, it fails, because replaying nothing would look like a pass.
# PIPELINE_BROWSER_USE_REPLAY_URLS_PATH=/absolute/path/to/failing-urls.json
